    "id": "sitl12-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 38 Signing",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "MAVLink2 signing against the standalone companion ArduCopter (sysid 20). Harness injects passphrase hunter11 and SETUP_SIGNING before deploy — see tab comment.",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl12-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl12-tab",
    "name": "MAVLink 2 signing (companion AP sysid 20)",
    "info": "Connection: sign outbound + require signed inbound. Passphrase credential is hunter11 (joke lab secret — not for production).\n\nLab harness (sitl/run-example-suite.js):\n1. docker-restarts the fleet; proves companion AP-20 arm-ready; then SETUP_SIGNING with sha256(hunter11).\n2. Deploys this flow with Admin API credentials: { signingPassphrase: \"hunter11\" }.\n3. Injects arm; expects COMMAND_ACK accepted and mavlink-in msg.trusted === true on HEARTBEAT.\n\nPorts: bind 0.0.0.0:14540 → remote 127.0.0.1:14541 (companion AP, not the GCS fleet on 14550).\n\nArm-ready must precede SETUP_SIGNING — after the key is loaded, unsigned commands are rejected on non-COMM_0 links (SITL udpclient is not guaranteed to be COMM_0).\n\nSigning is off by default in all other examples.",
    "x": 300,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
